This is deliberately more permissive than a brand licence usually is.
Derivatives are allowed on purpose: the celery can be redrawn, recoloured,
animated, stickered, or taken somewhere nobody has thought of yet. A mascot
a community cannot touch is not much of a mascot.

Attribute as:

    celeritty logo — https://github.com/edjubert/celeritty — CC BY 4.0

The rest of the repository is Apache-2.0; see ../LICENSE.


WHAT THIS DOES NOT GRANT

Copyright and trademark are separate things. The licence above covers the
artwork as a creative work. It grants no right in the name "celeritty", nor
in the marks as marks. Use them to refer to this project — not to brand a
different one, and not in any way that suggests this project endorses yours.
